    "https://www.oxy.edu/student-life/career-services": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services | Occidental College Skip to main content Menu Apply Visit Request Info Menu Career Services Home Student Life Career Services Your career journey starts at Occidental, where you’ll find support to help you explore possibilities, build skills, and take your next step with confidence. The Hameetman Career Center (HCC) works with students throughout their time at Oxy and continues to serve them as alumni. Career development is an ongoing process, whether you’re just beginning to consider what interests you, looking for an internship, preparing for your first job, or thinking about continuing your education. Through personalized advising and career counseling, programs, resources, and connections with employers and alumni, the Career Center helps you explore career paths, gain practical experience, hone professional skills, and translate your Oxy education into opportunities beyond the College. You’ll graduate with greater clarity about your goals and the confidence and experience to pursue them. 65% Oxy students who participate in internships 80% medical school acceptance rate, 2020-25 In This Section For Students Career Education Internship Programs InternLA Program Graduate Studies For Alumni For Employers Career Services FAQs First Destination Survey Meet Our Team Related Links National & International Fellowships Pre-Health Advising Pre-Law Advising Handshake Handshake is Occidental’s career platform for students and alumni, bringing job and internship opportunities, career events, employer connections, and helpful resources together in one place. Log in to Handshake Start Your Career Journey Explore options through Oxy’s career education series The Career Education Series offers career support by helping you explore a wide range of career paths and discover how your academic interests, skills, and experiences can translate into real-world opportunities. Meet with a career adviser one-on-one Career support and advising is available to every Oxy student, whether you’re just getting started, have a specific question, or want guidance along the way. Our career services team is excited to help you explore your options and plot your next steps. Explore internship and job opportunities Oxy connects students and alumni with internships, jobs, and a wide network of employers. Through Handshake , Oxy’s career platform, you can explore professional opportunities and connect with employers. Visit our internships page to learn about unique Oxy programs. Considering graduate studies? The HCC supports students interested in pursuing graduate or professional education as they explore options that fit their goals. Get guidance on researching programs, navigating the application process, and preparing application materials. Occidental Career Outcome Stories Anissa Basnayake ’25 Cognitive Science, Neuroscience MPhil, Ethics of AI, Data & Algorithms, University of Cambridge “My undergraduate experience at Occidental was invaluable—teaching me  how to critically engage and evaluate our world, encouraging me to pursue interests in the intersection of AI/big tech and human rights, and providing opportunities for me to explore vigorous cross-disciplinary studies.” Ethan Glass '19 Media Arts & Culture, Economics CEO & Co-founder, Ocra “Students have the opportunity to hone vital skills at Oxy. The leadership skills developed from co-captaining the Men's Soccer Team and the storytelling prowess taught in the Media Arts department contribute daily to my profession.” Forbes 30 Under 30 Announcement Marissa Chan '17 Urban & Environmental Policy Doctoral program, Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health “A liberal arts degree allows you to develop as not only a student but also a person who is able to give back. Both my coursework and my professors helped with that.” Read Oxy Story Meet More Alumni Career Support for Alumni Career support at Oxy includes resources to help young alumni navigate career transitions, explore new directions, and connect with the Oxy network. Alumni can access career counseling, job opportunities, events, and other resources through Handshake for up to three years after graduating. Access Alumni Support Employers: Recruit Oxy Talent The Career Center connects employers directly with Oxy students and alumni who are ready to bring their skills and perspectives to the workplace. Recruit Oxy talent by posting jobs and internships, participating in on-campus events, and building connections with our community. Recruit Oxy Students Contact  Career Services Hameetman Career Center AGC 109, F-34 1600 Campus Road / Los Angeles, CA 90041 Interactive Map to HCC Office Hours: 9 - 5 pm, Mon - Fri Phone: (323) 259-2623 careers@oxy.edu Follow us 1600 Campus Road Los Angeles, California 90041 (323) 259-2500 Follow Oxy: FACEBOOK INSTAGRAM YOUTUBE Linkedin Working at Oxy Accreditation Contact Us Civil Rights & Title IX Maps & Directions Disability Services Disclosures & Consumer Info © Copyright 2026. Occidental College. All Rights Reserved. Apply Visit Request Info Menu Close Apply Visit Request Info About Oxy Oxy Stories Career Outcomes Los Angeles Sustainability Community Engagement Admission Why Occidental? Affordability First-Year Admission Transfer Admission Int'l Admission Financial Aid Cost of Attendance How Aid Works How to Apply for Aid For Current Students Academics Areas of Study Our Faculty Student Research Global Engagement Student Success Student Life Housing Campus Dining Athletics & Wellness Career Services Get Involved Search Search Info For Alumni Faculty & Staff Second column Students Parents & Family Popular Searches Giving Library Academic Calendar Marketplace Bookstore Registrar Arts at Oxy Maps & Directions Oxy News Event Calendar Quick Links MyOxy Athletics Admission Portal Canvas Oxy ARTS Academic Catalog"
    }
